WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.810
- Hi, I'm Drew Barrymore,

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:05.410
and I just wanna say to
all the moms out there

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:09.450
that I get it, I know what
being a mom is all about,

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:13.330
and it is the greatest
thing you will ever do.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:15.430
It's also incredibly hard.

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:19.960
Heart strings pulled, laughs
galore, hair tearing out.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.980
Oh my God, it's everything.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:26.019
But it is the greatest love
I have or will ever know.

00:00:26.019 --> 00:00:28.602
(upbeat music)

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.600
- Hi everyone, I'm Chelsea Clinton.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.070
I'm a mom of three.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:35.580
- Hi everyone, I'm Cynthia Germanotta,

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.520
and I have two amazing daughters.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.280
Stefani, who you may know as Lady Gaga,

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:44.160
and Natalie who is a wonderful
and up and coming designer.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.440
- Hi, I'm Ali Wentworth.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:48.280
I have two adorable teenage daughters.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.610
- Hey guys, I'm Molly Sims,

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:52.120
and to all the mothers out there,

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:54.210
we all know that motherhood

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:57.580
is actually not always glamorous.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:59.810
- I have vivid memories of the first time

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:03.370
each of my three children
peed all over me.

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:06.630
One, it was while I was
trying to give him a bath,

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:08.410
and it just went boop right up on me.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:12.840
One, I was trying to change
a diaper, similar trajectory.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:15.470
And for my daughter, I thought I could

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:18.000
like change her diaper
while she was standing up,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.720
and that didn't work out
really for her or for me.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.550
And yet I wouldn't trade any of them

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.580
for anything in the world.

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:27.300
- To all your moms out there,

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.260
trust me, I know that
motherhood is not always easy,

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:34.150
but I have to say it's
what I love the most.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:36.210
It's how I identify the most.

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:39.890
What I do wanna say though,
is as my daughters get older

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:41.500
I still just wanna be a mom.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.790
So maybe I fall into that
category of helicopter mom,

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:49.400
and they're frequently reminding
me, "Mom, we got this."

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.210
So I'm learning to back off.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.640
It's one of the hardest
things that I've ever done,

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:54.770
but I have to understand

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:56.610
and respect that they're grown women

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:59.490
and let them go out into the
world and do their thing.

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:01.960
- I remember years ago on Mother's Day,

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:06.960
I was sitting in bed waiting
for cards, candy, flowers.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:11.900
I got a post-it note that
said, "Love you Mama."

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.990
So I had a emergency family meeting,

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:16.770
and I called in my husband,
George and the two daughters,

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:20.000
and I had to educate
them about Mother's Day.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.870
And it might have been
a little passionate,

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:26.870
because I said I live and
breathe and bleed for you,

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:30.450
so I expect a little
bit of love in return.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:34.070
So all I can tell you is
it's a work in progress.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:37.150
- I have very young kids.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:39.300
I have a just turned five year old,

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.290
six year old, and nine year old.

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:44.450
And I thought we haven't been skiing.

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:47.920
COVID, haven't really done
a lot, traveled a lot,

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.910
let's go skiing.

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:52.050
Let me tell you, the struggle was real.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:55.020
None of them know how to
ski, which was really fun

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:58.640
when you have three kids,
three different ages

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.310
and none know how to ski.

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:01.290
They don't like their boots.

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:02.190
They don't like their gear.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:03.880
They don't like their mom.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:06.550
We ended up having a fantastic time.

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:10.220
I literally carried them up the mountain.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:11.980
The struggle was real.

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:12.813
I love them.

00:03:12.813 --> 00:03:14.400
I love them dearly.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.880
But let me tell you something,

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.510
I needed a drink, I needed 10 drinks.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:21.030
Motherhood, it's so fun.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:23.750
I think that's why I hide in my closet

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:24.780
with my husband sometimes,

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:28.477
and we have like a date
without the kids in my closet.

00:03:28.477 --> 00:03:30.070
(tongue clicking) It's true.

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:32.750
- So it may not always be cute or easy-

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:34.620
- But it's always worth it-

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:38.180
- And I'm excited to celebrate
moms this Mother's Day.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:40.570
- Thanks for having
me, happy Mother's Day.

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.600
- Just the happiest, happiest, happiest,

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:43.710
healthiest Mother's Day

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:46.410
to all the hardworking moms everywhere.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:47.860
- Happy Mother's Day, Drew,

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.580
and to all the mothers out there.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.070
- It is truly the best.

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:52.290
And I miss my mom.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.620
- Thank you for having me, Drew.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:54.890
- Happy Mother's Day.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:56.410
It takes a village.

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:58.069
It takes a city really.

00:03:58.069 --> 00:04:00.652
(upbeat music)

